WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.563
Nearly a quarter gone.

00:00:01.573 --> 00:00:02.495
One day.

00:00:02.505 --> 00:00:06.639
October 19, 1987, Black Monday:

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:09.044
the Dow fell 22.6%.

00:00:09.144 --> 00:00:11.849
It's still the largest
one-day percentage fall

00:00:11.859 --> 00:00:13.093
in the Dow's history.

00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:14.512
And it got worse:

00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:17.902
computer-based portfolio
insurance likely sped the fall

00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:20.865
up, as early losses triggered more rounds

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:21.694
of selling.

00:00:21.704 --> 00:00:23.756
Next morning, the Fed said it was

00:00:23.766 --> 00:00:25.819
ready to supply the cash the system

00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:26.704
needed.

00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:29.179
So how long did recovery take?

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:30.786
Less than two years.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:33.498
By 1989, US stocks were back above

00:00:33.508 --> 00:00:35.466
their pre-crash highs.
